{"skill":{"slug":"stock-watcher","displayName":"Stock Watcher"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770348343954,"changelog":"Stock Watcher Skill – Initial Release\n\n- Manage a personal stock watchlist: add, remove, list, and clear stocks using 6-digit codes.\n- View concise summaries of recent stock performance with real-time data from 10jqka.com.cn.\n- Directly display key metrics and provide links for detailed information on each stock.\n- Fully supports A-share markets, including Shanghai, Shenzhen, and STAR Market.\n- Command-line scripts included for all core operations with consistent configuration management.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":3152,"sha256":"64ffed610197e88f1d2574e458e29ff92f2fe882aa7dabfa77468612b16326e0","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2906,"sha256":"4d7b3616d674e7f11a79b6f491a06108f2ffcc0d7f107c4d6107f056eac494a6","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/add_stock.py","size":2801,"sha256":"bca743d747731e33154aa8851a0ebe161d6062381c6deb6c445c4fac40cf265f","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/clear_watchlist.py","size":664,"sha256":"27aecee130f51eef022fb0e8e46995749d791677a80daa77e52787ffb2f8d60f","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/config.py","size":361,"sha256":"e36d2be7cb0f5df8d6915c3cb6d0d3b4dfe52ede0dbe0d9ccc7cc1ab75e61a8b","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/install.sh","size":903,"sha256":"03bb45d2c74cbef0cbd0a950df14b859cdecdc5f6550a3d7fb3e753faa2095cd","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/list_stocks.py","size":981,"sha256":"662e3bb19198d30a619a99b4ff7969bc153f0c32784e6f8ccb5e6d5d4d05ab79","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/remove_stock.py","size":1493,"sha256":"236ce33527f7a2afd39a939fa89b1d44bd3b0351ed4112d5c4271947bee84ef8","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/summarize_performance.py","size":3447,"sha256":"7e8c67dae066e923ecfdd7393ef35ee3f14a54ffd912f51eb77f7ba22312fa7e","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/uninstall.sh","size":310,"sha256":"c943b43a17c1212aec968a0368286d8cbbb8ecfd4c9d654941314c78f3257096","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2198,"sha256":"d8824e8af3b132d9c9fd0853452b2db682c1ef9ba4978a6ec351540c2405893a","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789036352555,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"d47491d77aad5a8c0fb0f6436bb265317e4d5159bce2ec71cd1d264142add9e4","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/d47491d77aad5a8c0fb0f6436bb265317e4d5159bce2ec71cd1d264142add9e4","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: stock-watcher\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe OpenClaw AgentSkills skill bundle 'stock-watcher' is benign. All scripts (Python and Bash) and documentation clearly align with the stated purpose of managing a stock watchlist and fetching public stock data from 10jqka.com.cn. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts against the agent. File operations are confined to the skill's designated data directory (`~/.clawdbot/stock_watcher/watchlist.txt`), and network requests are exclusively to the specified stock data source.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161770510},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":71,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":9,"checkedAt":1789036352555},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill matches its stated stock-watchlist purpose and is scoped to its own local watchlist data, but users should notice that clear and uninstall actions can erase saved entries.","dimensions":[{"detail":"File access is limited to the skill's own watchlist directory, and network requests go to a declared stock-data host constructed from watchlist stock codes.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The install script creates ~/.clawdbot/stock_watcher and an empty watchlist file, and only warns about missing Python packages; documentation suggests unpinned requests and beautifulsoup4 installation.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Instructions identify the local watchlist path and stock-data host, with no prompt hijacking or hidden role changes found; they do not provide an explicit permissions section or confirmation requirements for destructive actions.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill keeps a persistent watchlist file as expected for a watchlist manager, but it installs no cron jobs, services, shell profile hooks, credential access, or privilege escalation mechanisms.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifacts coherently implement adding, removing, listing, clearing, and summarizing a personal Chinese A-share watchlist using 10jqka.com.cn data; clearing and uninstall deletion are purpose-related but destructive.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable with a local watchlist file under ~/.clawdbot/stock_watcher and network lookups to 10jqka.com.cn. Back up the watchlist before using clear or uninstall, because those flows can erase saved entries without confirmation. Prefer installing Python dependencies in a virtual environment with pinned versions.","findings":"[TP4] expected: The clear and uninstall behavior is destructive, but it concerns the skill's own watchlist data and is documented as part of watchlist management rather than hidden unrelated behavior.\n[SQP-2] expected: Clearing the watchlist and uninstalling can erase saved entries without an in-script confirmation; this is a real safety/usability issue, but the scope is limited to local watchlist data and does not by itself warrant Review.\n[LP3] expected: The skill lacks a formal permissions section, but the artifact text and code consistently show a narrow local data path and a declared network source.\n[RA2] expected: Creating ~/.clawdbot/stock_watcher/watchlist.txt is normal state for a watchlist skill; inspection found no scheduled task, service, startup hook, or background persistence.\n[SQP-3] expected: Chinese instructions and output are consistent with a Chinese A-share tracker using a Chinese market data site, though language preference support could be improved.\n[T08] unexpected: The unpinned dependency guidance is a supply-chain hygiene concern, but it references common packages and does not fetch or execute a hidden remote payload.\n[T09] unexpected: The add script does not enforce the documented six-digit code or sanitize delimiters/control characters, which could corrupt or misdisplay watchlist records but remains confined to the skill's local data and fixed host requests.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789036352555}}}}}